# fixedbugs, defect 559, lane b18-ffi, 2026-10-10 (panel 202's C0; the
# compiler-engineer's `fprec`).
#
# A group record beside a `static inline twice` of `int`, in a program whose
# other module binds a `twice` of `long long` from its own header. Each module's
# unit compiles alone. Until 2026-10-10 every module's unit read every group
# record's header, and the layout check read every header of the program in
# one unit, so this was refused, *the headers two groups name cannot be
# compiled in one unit*, while the program without the record built. A
# module's unit reads its own groups' headers now, and it builds.
use fixedbugs559/long_twice

extern "fixedbugs-559-int.h"
    record Pt
        v: i32
    function twice(x: i32) -> i32
    function ptv(p: Pt) -> i32

function main()
    print(long_twice.doubled(x: 3))
    print(twice(x: 4) + ptv(p: Pt(v: 1)))
